Requirements (25 requirements needed)
FRO1: [BRIEF] This system will allow students to book support appointments.

FRO2: [BRIEF] The system shall allow students to select the support category they need.

FRO3: [CANDIDATE] The system shall allow students to reschedule or cancel appointments.

FRO4: [CANDIDATE] The system shall notify a student if the appointment booking is unsuccessful.

FRO5: [CANDIDATE?] The system shall restrict appointment availability to students.

FRO6: [CANDIDATE?] The system shall only allow the student and support staff to view the booked appointment.

FRO7: [BRIEF] The system will allow students to request a specific staff member if they are available

FRO8: [BRIEF] The system will notify both the student and staff member on event of a successful booking.

FRO9: [CANDIDATE] The system shall notify both student and staff member upon a successfull booking

FRO10: [CANDIDATE?] The system will remove already-booked appointment slots.

FRO11: [BRIEF] The system shall manage staff availability.
 
FRO12: [BRIEF] The system will send a reminder to both students and support staff prior to the appointment.

FRO13: [CANDIDATE] The system will enable the booked staff member to record if a student attends or doesn't attend

FRO14: [BRIEF] The system will allow support staff to block off specific times, days or weeks.

FRO15: [CANDIDATE] The system will require all users to authenticate based on the colleges sign-in system.

FRO16: [CANDIDATE] The system should allow students to view previous and upcoming appointments.

FRO17: [CANDIDATE?] The system shall allow students to input a reason for booking the appointment.

FRO18: [CANDIDATE] The system will let admins to manage all accounts and permissions.

FRO19: [CANDIDATE] The system will notify the student if their appointment is cancelled.

NFR01: The system will conform to industry WCAG 2.1 accessibility standards.

NFR02: System will have load times under 2 seconds.

NFR03: The system shall follow standard industry architecture and use a suitable framework.

NFR04: [CANDIDATE?] Maintenance for the system may only occur outside of academic hours e.g. 00:00 - 05:00.

NFR05: [CANDIDATE] A first-time student should be able to find and book an available appointment without guidance.

NFR06: [CANDIDATE] The system will follow rigid design patterns to guarantee easy usability for students

NFR07: [CANDIDATE] The system should have accurate appointment information.


